  "description": "USN-8952-2 fixed a regression in Tornado that broke static file serving\nfor applications that subclass Tornado's StaticFileHandler, such as\nJupyter. Unfortunately, that update's incomplete fix could introduce a regression by rejecting symlinks into system\ndirectories like /usr/share, which distribution packages use for their\nJavaScript and fonts, causing web UIs to return 403 errors. This update\nfixes the problem.\n\nWe apologize for the inconvenience.\n\nOriginal advisory details:\n\n It was discovered that Tornado did not properly handle certain HTTP requests\n and network inputs. An attacker could possibly use these issues to cause a\n denial of service, expose sensitive information, or bypass access controls.\n\n (CVE-2023-54397, CVE-2024-14029, CVE-2026-91990, CVE-2026-91992,\n CVE-2026-103262, CVE-2026-103263)",
